aling to Physical AoE damage; alternative support set.","stats":"HP%/ER · HP% · HP%"}],"t":[{"name":"Nefer Nation","members":["Baizhu","Nefer","Columbina","Lauma"],"text":"Nefer leads with powerful Lunar-Bloom damage, while Lauma and Columbina provide reaction support and Hydro application. Baizhu keeps the team healthy.","roles":["Healer / Shielder","On-field DPS","Off-field DPS / Buffer","Dendro Buffer / Enabler"]},{"name":"Dendro Dominance","members":["Baizhu","Alhaitham","Yae Miko","Fischl"],"text":"Alhaitham drives Spread damage while Yae and Fischl provide consistent Electro application and off-field damage.","roles":["Healer / Shielder","On-field DPS","Off-field DPS","Off-field DPS / Battery"]},{"name":"Nilou's Garden","members":["Baizhu","Kamisato Ayato","Nilou","Nahida"],"text":"Nilou transforms Bloom reactions into devastating Bountiful Cores.","roles":["Healer / Shielder","On-field DPS","Bloom Buffer / Hydro Enabler","Dendro Enabler / Buffer"]},{"name":"Bloom & Doom","members":["Baizhu","Kaveh","Xingqiu","Nilou"],"text":"Nilou enables powerful Bountiful Core reactions, while Kaveh acts as the on-field Dendro driver.","roles":["Healer / Shielder","On-field Driver","Off-field DPS / Hydro Enabler","Bloom Buffer / Hydro Enabler"]}],"v":"Deepwood Dendro Support: Use Baizhu to heal and shred Dendro RES, enabling more damage from Dendro and Bloom-based teams.\nAlternate Healing / Buffs: Choose Song of Days Past for healing-based buffs or Clam for modest extra bubble damage.\nOn-field Dendro Driver: Use Normal Attacks to apply Dendro for Bloom or Hyperbloom while maintaining team healing.","n":4},"seo":{"roles":["Support"],"about":"Baizhu is a Dendro healer who provides strong team-wide healing, interruption resistance, and Dendro application. He offers valuable defensive utility while supporting Dendro reactions.","pros":["Strong team healing","Dendro reaction buffs","Teamwide sustain","Flexible support"],"cons":["Fragile shields","Limited Dendro aura","High ER needs","Low personal DMG"],"weapons":["Jadefall's Splendor","Prototype Amber","A Thousand Floating Dreams","Everlasting Moonglow","Favonius Codex","Sacrificial Fragments","Hakushin Ring","Thrilling Tales of Dragon Slayers"],"arts":[{"sets":["Deepwood Memories"],"pcs":"4 pcs","role":"Best Support"},{"sets":["Song of Days Past"],"pcs":"4 pcs","role":"Support"},{"sets":["Ocean-Hued Clam"],"pcs":"4 pcs","role":"Support"}],"main":["HP% / ER","HP%","HP% / Healing"],"stats":["HP: Up to 50K","ER: Team-based","CR: Favonius only"],"vars":[{"title":"Deepwood Dendro Support","role":"Healer / Support","weapons":["Jadefall's Splendor","Prototype Amber","Favonius Codex"],"arts":[{"sets":["Deepwood Memories"],"pcs":"4 pcs"}],"stats":"Meet ER needs, then build HP% toward 50,000. A CRIT Circlet is optional with Favonius.","teams":"Dendro damage teams without another reliable Deepwood holder.","when":"Use Baizhu to heal and shred Dendro RES, enabling more damage from Dendro and Bloom-based teams.","cond":"Deepwood is less valuable if another teammate maintains its RES shred.","notes":"","pre":false},{"title":"Alternate Healing / Buffs","role":"Healer / Support","weapons":["Prototype Amber","Jadefall's Splendor","Favonius Codex"],"arts":[{"sets":["Song of Days Past"],"pcs":"4 pcs"},{"sets":["Ocean-Hued Clam"],"pcs":"4 pcs"}],"stats":"HP% and ER stay the priority; Healing Bonus is an optional comfort choice.","teams":"A teammate already carries Deepwood, or Dendro RES shred is not needed.","when":"Choose Song of Days Past for healing-based buffs or Clam for modest extra bubble damage.","cond":"Prioritize support uptime over personal damage.","notes":"","pre":false},{"title":"On-field Dendro Driver","role":"On-field Driver","weapons":["Prototype Amber","Sacrificial Fragments","Favonius Codex"],"arts":[{"sets":["Deepwood Memories"],"pcs":"4 pcs"}],"stats":"EM can help only when Baizhu owns Bloom reactions; otherwise HP and ER usually remain more useful.","teams":"Hydro and/or Electro units for Dendro reactions; reliable healing.","when":"Use Normal Attacks to apply Dendro for Bloom or Hyperbloom while maintaining team healing.","cond":"Hyperbloom damage scales with the Electro trigger’s EM, not Baizhu’s.","notes":"","pre":false}],"mats":["Nagadus Emerald Sliver","Nagadus Emerald Fragment","Nagadus Emerald Chunk","Nagadus Emerald Gemstone","Evergloom Ring","Teachings of Gold","Guide to Gold","Philosophies of Gold","Fungal Spores","Luminescent Pollen","Crystalline Cyst Dust","Violetgrass","Worldspan Fern","Crown of Insight","Mora","Hero's Wit"],"talents":[{"name":"Normal Attack","pri":"Level 1+"},{"name":"Elemental Skill","pri":"Level 9+"},{"name":"Elemental Burst","pri":"Level 9+"}],"teams":[{"name":"Nefer Nation","members":["Baizhu","Nefer","Columbina","Lauma"]},{"name":"Dendro Dominance","members":["Baizhu","Alhaitham","Yae Miko","Fischl"]},{"name":"Nilou's Garden","members":["Baizhu","Kamisato Ayato","Nilou","Nahida"]},{"name":"Bloom & Doom","members":["Baizhu","Kaveh","Xingqiu","Nilou"]}]}}],"title":"Baizhu","el":"Dendro"}